==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-read in.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,read>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[accept]] as [[input]].
#: {{ux|en|The computer '''reads in''' a program file from disk and executes the contents.}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To [[allow]] [[access]] to [[classified]] [[information]].
#: {{ux|en|― What is this?<br /> ― I can tell you what this isn't. This isn't me '''reading''' you '''in''', Bernard.}}
# {{lb|en|law}} To judicially insert an official legal interpretation into a [[statute]]<ref>{{cite-web |title=SECTION 1 OF THE CHARTER AND THE OAKES TEST |url=https://ojen.ca/wp-content/uploads/In-Brief_Section-1-and-Oakes_0.pdf |work=Ontario Justice Education Network|year=2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260901051241/https://ojen.ca/wp-content/uploads/In-Brief_Section-1-and-Oakes_0.pdf|archivedate=1 September 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web |title=Reading in |url=https://irwinlaw.com/cold/reading-in/ |work=Irwin Law|year=2021|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250320023007/https://irwinlaw.com/cold/reading-in/|archivedate=20 March 2025}}</ref>

